<title>USA: Martin Marietta Materials acqusition wins approval.</title>
<headline>Martin Marietta Materials acqusition wins approval.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Justice Department Tuesday gave permission for Martin Marietta Materials Inc to acquire American Aggregates Corp for $234.5 million, if it sells a quarry in Indianapolis, Indiana.</p>
<p>Martin Marietta Materials must sell American Aggregates' Harding Street Quarry. Aggregate is used to manufacture roads.</p>
<p>The settlement, filed in U.S. District Court in Indianaplois, will now be open to a 60-day comment period.</p>
</text>
